{
 "id": "p2-w15-m1",
 "title": "Row storage makes you read everything",
 "alt": "A whiteboard sketch showing a CSV drawn as seven rows of eight shaded cells where seven of every eight cells are struck through as wasted, annotated that a sum over one column still reads all 663.3 megabytes; Parquet drawn as eight vertical strips whose widths are the real compressed column sizes from 69.5 megabytes for the timestamp down to 0.5 for a boolean, with only the 20.9 megabyte amount strip shaded; the same file split into ten row groups where nine are struck through in red because the footer statistics proved they cannot contain matching rows; and measured bars showing count star at 0.43 seconds on CSV against 0.0019 on Parquet, and sum of amount at 0.78 against 0.047.",
